{
  "case_id": "2016-15-577",
  "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "David A. Cortman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State of Missouri has excluded The Learning Center from a recycling program that provides a safer playground for children solely because the preschool is operated by a church rather than a secular not-for-profit. The State has made several important concessions in this case. Number one, that the policy in this case is not facially neutral, and number two, that based on their religious character, churches are not eligible for the benefit here. This admitted discrimination against religion violates this Court's Free Exercise Principles."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Assuming that there's no serious risk of an establishment violation, that's off the table, are there ever instances in which status -- religious status can be used to deny religions or religious believers benefits from the State? Or are you saying that it's -- that absent in Establishment Clause problem, that status can never be the base -- religious status can never be the basis for a governmental action or governmental ordinance, governmental statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On that -- on that question, I guess rather long ago now in the Everson case back in 1947, this Court said in no uncertain terms what the Framers didn't want was tax money imposed to pay for building or maintaining churches or church property. And doesn't that fit this case? And if so, is Everson pass\u00e9?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So how is the building separate from the religious exercise therein? I believe that this playground is part of the ministry of this church. And, in fact, I look at its bylaws, I look at its advertisements, and it includes play and conducted in a religiously valuable way. I think that's the materials that you're -- that the church is advertising. How do you separate out its secular function from its religious function?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David A. Cortman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the way the Court always has. And the answer to that is, for example, even though the motivation behind operating this preschool is a religious motivation, doesn't mean that every single activity that occurs there happens to be religious."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David A. Cortman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As was mentioned in one of the amicus briefs, I believe it was the World Vision brief, the surfacing being softer doesn't enable religious activities, it doesn't allow it, it doesn't prohibit it. It's really completely separate and apart from it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David A. Cortman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They are. And interestingly in this case, the State concedes, and as did the lower court, there is no Federal Establishment Clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that that is the proper way to analyze this question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that that is the proper way to analyze this question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cortman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't. And -- and this -- this particular provision that we're discussing, they are -- and this has been briefed by several amicus briefs and -- and briefly by us, is a product of what we would consider to be one of the Blaine Amendments that was not found in Locke v. Davey. And the reason for that is, is it has that same language in the Blaine Amendment. It was adopted the same exact year, and there is much history showing about the anti-Catholic bigotry that's behind this specific provision, and"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cortman",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because I don't think this is one of the difficult cases. In fact, I would say, with all the Court's jurisprudence under Free Exercise and Establishment Clause, this is actually one of the easier cases. And the reason for that is if you look at the play in joints, the first conclusion was there was no Free Exercise violation there. Here, there clearly is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Layton",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes. Yes. We don't want to be in a position, for example, in this case, where we are selecting among churches. We don't want to be in a position where we are making a visible, physical improvement on church property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm asking, does the Constitution of the United States permit a State or a city to say, we give everybody in this city police protection, but not churches? We give everybody fire protection, but let the church burn down. We give everybody public health protection, but not a church. That's -- that's the law in my imaginary State. And I'm saying, does the Constitution, which guarantees free exercise of religion, permit such laws?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Why in health context? So\nif there's --\nMR. LAYTON: No."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Layton",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So we start on the endorsement side. In\nthose instances, the State is not endorsing a particular\nchurch by choosing to provide that church with those\nbenefits and not another church, which is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Mr. Layton, let's say I -- I accept\nthat the State might have an interest in\nsaying we just don't want to be seen as giving money to\none church and not another in these selective programs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Layton",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have a church that, in order to participate,\nhas to agree to curriculum requirements in their\npreschool."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "in this particular program, the church gets points for\ntelling people in the community that the State paid for\nthis improvement to their church."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: But how do we draw the line between selective and general? One -- one could seem to play with that line forever."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David A. Cortman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "097c5fdbc8edae1e6d80f543c09692341c7290d7231589afa3bf6386a4fe6ba7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-097c5fdbc8ed-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First of all, as to the endorsement problem, I think the neutral government criteria here take care of the endorsement problem. So when you have this competitive grant that you have to fill out this -- this pretty complicated application, 16 neutral criteria, there is no endorsement of religion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-577",
      "confidence": 0.0,
